# Code owners for github.com/dotcomjack/grux
#
# On a solo repository this does nothing today: GitHub never requests a review from the
# author of a pull request, so it costs Jack nothing on his own changes. It exists for
# the first outside contributor, and specifically for the two directories where an
# unreviewed change is expensive.
#
# Sources/ and Tests/ are the tagged, cold-resolve-proven tree behind 0.6.1. The suite is
# the product's evidence, so a change to Tests/ that quietly relaxes an assertion is as
# serious as a change to Sources/ that introduces a leak. Both are named here for that
# reason, and the security policy and the corpus contract are named for the same one.
#
# CODEOWNERS only has teeth with branch protection requiring review from code owners, so
# turn that on when the repository goes public.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below wins. Last match takes precedence.
*                       @dotcomjack

# The library itself.
/Sources/               @dotcomjack

# The evidence. 115 tests, and the corpus contract that defines correct.
/Tests/                 @dotcomjack

# The published promises. Each of these is quoted somewhere a stranger reads it.
/SECURITY.md            @dotcomjack
/README.md              @dotcomjack
/CHANGELOG.md           @dotcomjack
/LICENSE                @dotcomjack

# Build and release surface. Package.swift carries the platform floor, and a change to
# the workflow can turn a real gate into one that only looks like a gate.
/Package.swift          @dotcomjack
/.github/               @dotcomjack
